    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_core_one_exceptional_only_distance_three_quartic_boundary_crt_reconstruction",
    "title": "Rate-half distance-three quartic boundary CRT reconstruction",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the exact distance-three design, the pair labels define delta=xi_i modulo D_i in F[X]/(A), and the first-jet sum sum_i D_iN_iL_i is divisible by z-delta. Multiplication of its quotient by the explicit smooth-domain derivative factor reconstructs the global quartic Omega coefficientwise modulo A. A valid packet forces the generic degree-<2e remainder to collapse to X-degree at most four; within the active-row design this collapse is equivalent to the global quartic weld. No projective-line or splitting claim is made.",
